#: includes/abilities/media/upload-media.php:287
msgid "The filename must end in an image or video extension this site accepts, such as .jpg, .png, .webp or .mp4. SVG files are not supported."
msgstr "The filename must end in an image or video extension this site accepts, such as .jpg, .png, .webp or .mp4. SVG files are not supported."

#: includes/abilities/media/upload-media.php:279
msgid "A filename with its extension is required to get an upload link. Pass source_url instead to add a file from a public URL."
msgstr "A filename with its extension is required to get an upload link. Pass source_url instead to add a file from a public URL."

#: includes/abilities/media/upload-media.php:163
msgid "Run it from your code-execution sandbox or shell with the file path filled in. The response is the stored attachment. An HTML 413 page means the web server allows smaller uploads than max_bytes. A 401 or 403 with a code other than premium_addons_* (such as rest_not_logged_in) means a security plugin blocks logged-out REST requests, so this site cannot take uploads this way. In that case, or without a shell or code execution, ask the user for a public URL or to upload the file in WordPress instead."
msgstr "Run it from your code-execution sandbox or shell with the file path filled in. The response is the stored attachment. An HTML 413 page means the web server allows smaller uploads than max_bytes. A 401 or 403 with a code other than premium_addons_* (such as rest_not_logged_in) means a security plugin blocks logged-out REST requests, so this site cannot take uploads this way. In that case, or without a shell or code execution, ask the user for a public URL or to upload the file in WordPress instead."

